    "result_text": "There's only one test in the suite and it passes. Build is green.\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented the `timezone` field on the owner response, derived from the locality/region via the fixed region-to-timezone table.\n\n**Changes:**\n\n1. **`src/main/resources/openapi.yml`** \u2014 Added a read-only `timezone` string field to the owner schema (after `locality`), documenting the IANA-name derivation. `OwnerDto` is generated from this spec, so this creates the field/getter/setter.\n\n2. **`CityRegions.java`** (the single source of the region facts) \u2014 Added a `REGION_TIMEZONE` table (`NSW\u2192Australia/Sydney`, `VIC\u2192Australia/Melbourne`, `QLD\u2192Australia/Brisbane`) and a `timezoneOf(region)` lookup returning `null` for unknown regions.\n\n3. **`OwnerMapper.java`** \u2014 Added `@Mapping(target = \"timezone\", ...)` and a `toTimezone(owner)` method that resolves the region the same way as `locality` (`CityRegions.identityRegion(postcode)`) and maps it through `timezoneOf`, keeping timezone and locality consistent by construction.\n\nThe `AcceptanceTest.coreReturnsTimezoneForRegion` test (Sydney/postcode 2000 \u2192 locality `NSW`, timezone `Australia/Sydney`) passes, and the full suite builds green.",
