    "final_verdict": "VERDICT: LGTM\n\nThe change slots cleanly into the existing structure and reads as a natural extension of what's already there.\n\n- The region\u2192timezone fact lives in `CityRegions`, the single documented home of region facts, right beside `CITY_REGION` and `REGION_POSTCODES`. `timezoneOf(String region)` mirrors the existing `regionOf` / `postcodeRange` lookup accessors exactly (same signature shape, same null-when-unknown contract, same javadoc style). No new catch-all is introduced.\n- `OwnerMapper.toTimezone(Owner)` mirrors the sibling `toLocality(Owner)` / `toContactPreference(Owner)` `default` methods: one per derived field, taking `owner`, delegating to the shared model class. The `@Mapping` entry is placed logically right after `locality`, matching the derivation dependency.\n- No duplication of the table \u2014 the mapper delegates rather than re-encoding the mapping. `toTimezone` re-deriving the region via `identityRegion(...)` rather than calling `toLocality(owner)` is consistent with the codebase convention that each `toX(owner)` derives independently from the entity, and the javadoc cross-links the two so the shared-region intent is explicit.\n- The OpenAPI `timezone` property matches the surrounding `readOnly` derived-field entries in title/description/example format.\n\nLogic is in the right unit and a maintainer here would find it natural.",
